1. Add <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-amqp</artifactId> dependency in order-microservice.
2.   Add this configuration in order-microservice.yml
	rabbitmq:
		host: localhost
		port: 5672
		username: guest
		password: guest

	- Order service should know how to find Queue

3. Add these RabbitMQ properties in order-microservice.ymml
	# RAbbit MQ properties
rabbitmq:
  exchange:
    name: order.exchange
  queue:
    name: order.queue
  routing:
    key: order.tracking

4. Add RabbitMqConfiguration.java -This file wors as - setting up queue - exchange, binding it together, autoregistering @startup, Enabling the java objects as json and preparing Rabbitemplate to send messages.
5. Restart all services and docker-compose, and check - http://localhost:15672, -> Exchange -> "order.exchange".

6. Now we modify our OrderService.java, so once the order is placed, it sends an message to RabbitMQ-> Notification service.

7. Create notification-miroservice -
8. @Service
   public class OrderEventConsumer {
       // this can be read from yml file
       @RabbitListener(queues = "order.queue")
       public void handleOrderEvent(OrderCreatedEvent orderCreatedEvent){
           System.out.println("Received Order Event : " + orderCreatedEvent.toString());
       }
   }